hypoxia,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sleep"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fragmentation."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "The"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "obstruction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "typically"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "occurs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "at"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "level"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pharynx,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "often"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "due"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "collapse or anatomical narrowing involving ENT structures such as the adenoids, tonsils, nasal passages, soft palate, and base of "}, {"text": "tongue."}]}, {"id": "body-16301", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "In both children and adults, ENT-related anatomical factors contribute significantly to the pathophysiology of OSAS, and their recognition is critical for effective treatment planning.", "runs": [{"text": "In both children and adults, ENT-related anatomical factors contribute significantly to the pathophysiology of OSAS, and their recognition is critical for effective treatment planning."}]}, {"id": "body-16302", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "This section addresses only non-central sleep apnea. Central sleep apnea and non-Surgical treatment are discussed in the Respiratory and CNS chapters. ENT specialists play a key role in the multidisciplinary management of OSAS.", "runs": [{"text": "This section addresses only non-central sleep apnea. Central sleep apnea and non-Surgical treatment are discussed in the Respiratory and CNS chapters. ENT specialists play a key role in the multidisciplinary management of OSAS."}]}, {"id": "body-16305", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Etiology and Risk Factors", "runs": [{"text": "Etiology"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Risk"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Factors"}], "leve